<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Corn steady, soy offers firmer.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Corn steady, soy offers firmer.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. FOB Gulf corn steadied on Tuesday while soybean offers rose one to two cents a bushel, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Wheat values were unchanged.</p>
<p>In export news, Armenia is seeking about 65,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat under the PL 480 program for January 23-February 6 delivery, its U.S. export agent said.</p>
<p>Also, Taiwan will tender this Thursday for about 85,000 to 86,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat for January-February delivery, several U.S. exporters said.</p>
